{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/987986-rules-option-converting-mana-to-arcane-beats-for-a-cost","id":987986,"title":"Rules option: converting Mana to Arcane Beats for a cost.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-15T16:15:44-07:00","id":987986,"title":"Rules option: converting Mana to Arcane Beats for a cost.","content":"Just something I was thinking about while considering an updated Timori legacy. I like giving Nameless and other down-and-out mages fun stuff to play with. Let me know what you think!<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> <b>Supernal Communion</b><br /> Although it is frowned upon as wasteful and even dangerous by more conservative Diamond mages, the persistent desire for a quick path to power has kept this technique circulating among apprentices for centuries. It is more popular among low-Gnosis mages who have less to lose from it. Supernal Communion is a flash of revelation that forces a brief glimpse of Supernal truth, granting mystical insight at the cost of precious Mana.<br /> <br /> <b>Systems: </b>Supernal Communion may be used only when a mage has full Mana, whether their maximum capacity is 10 or 50. As an instant action, the mage spends all the Mana in their Pattern at once, ignoring the usual restrictions on Mana per turn. This causes their Immediate Nimbus to flare in the Fallen World as if they had activated it intentionally, with Strength equal to their Gnosis, and cannot be used if they have already flared their Nimbus in the same scene. The mage gains one Arcane Beat, and takes the Drained Condition and one resistant Lethal damage from the strain.<br /> <br /> <b>Drained</b><br /> Your character has had the Mana forcibly burned out of their system, and their Pattern is in withdrawal. While this Condition is active, your character does not regain Mana from performing Oblations, consuming Tass, or drawing on a Familiar. Pattern Scouring, fulfilling an Obsession, blood sacrifice, and other means of regaining Mana function normally. The mage may not cast Prime 3 &quot;Channel Mana&quot; to draw Mana into their own Pattern, but another mage may infuse them with Mana using the spell.<br /> <b>Resolution: </b>The mage regains their full Mana pool. This grants an Arcane Beat.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T16:24:19-07:00","id":987992,"title":"","content":"There are a number of ways to obtain infinite mana in Mage 2e. This seems very easy to break.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T16:46:13-07:00","id":988005,"title":"","content":"What if there was a flat cap on how often it can be used per day, like Pattern Scouring? And/or banned Channel Mana from a third party as well?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T23:45:37-07:00","id":988158,"title":"","content":"You might want to turn your attention to the sidebar on the bottom left of pg. 126 in the 2e book.<br /> <br /> My biggest problem with this isn't that it can be used to get experience points, it's that it doesn't do so in a way that seems evocative to me. Were I to make something like this, it would be a thing like Supernal Summoning: A path-based way to elevate an otherwise mundane experience to an arcane revelation. That way, you're doing more or less the same thing, but you have to do it appropriately for yourself... or, perhaps, for the person setting you on your way.<br /> <br /> I'd find &quot;Cast a mind spell that traps you in a Nightmare Play until you learn something important about yourself&quot; a lot more interesting to run for a Mastigos than a &quot;blow a fat wad of mana to get a beat.&quot; Similarly, see if the creative juices start flowing with the thought of &quot;Demand a quest for arcane knowledge from Fate itself.&quot; for Acanthus.<br /> <br /> Now, those would be a thing where you cast it to <i>definitely</i> get the experience. That's a pretty high level of the path's arcana, logically.<br /> <br /> A lesser form should be able to allow those who are doing things appropriate <i>already</i> to improve them into a superior lesson for Gnosis.<br /> You could ditch any need for a ritual to upgrade the lessons that fit a path, and simply make them hand out beats... possibly in parallel with the mundane forms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":672,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","user":"thenate","date":". 10-16-2016, 05:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T02:22:53-07:00","id":988192,"title":"","content":"I was going to point the Supernal Summoning, but <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar672_1.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"672\" data-vbnamecard=\"672\">thenate</a> has come first. I would only point that you <i>can</i> Supernal Summon without 3rd dot in Arcanum - it's just lot less secure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T04:00:31-07:00","id":988199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In order to summon a Supernal entity, the summoner must<br /> be of the Path corresponding to the type of entity desired and<br /> use one of her two Path Ruling Arcana, which she must have<br /> at least three dots in. </div> </div> </div>Page 95. You need three dots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}